<http://data.silknow.org/event/dc21a3e3-3888-3149-939e-20017278599d>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A note in the register says: 'this type of 'suba' is made in the Danube Valley especially about Gyongyos, where the industry has long been established and exports such coats to other parts of Hungary. A similar coat from (???) (in the Balkan district, SW Hungary) is illustrated in C. Viski 'L ARt Populaire Longroise (?)'.\n\nA later addition says 'this type of cloak is ultimately derived from the German Rud-mantel (?) of the 16th century of Numberg. (Festshnt (?) Hampe. 1926. p.12-13)."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/a6b82103-bddf-3e1a-97ac-a4d63ca13b98> ;
